{"id":"ed2d329f-b078-40ea-a1ed-30959a013ba7","object":"chat.completion","created":1784837327,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import json\\n    # Extract payload\\n    payload = case['payload'] if isinstance(case, dict) and 'payload' in case else case\\n    segments_data = payload['segments']\\n    budget = payload['budget']\\n    \\n    # Validate\\n    total_min = sum(seg['minimum'] for seg in segments_data)\\n    total_capacity = sum(seg['capacity'] for seg in segments_data)\\n    if budget < total_min or budget > total_capacity:\\n        raise ValueError('Budget infeasible')\\n    \\n    # Initialise allocations at minimum\\n    alloc = {seg['name']: seg['minimum'] for seg in segments_data}\\n    remaining = budget - total_min\\n    \\n    # Precompute importance and capacities per segment (keep order)\\n    names = [seg['name'] for seg in segments_data]\\n    importances = {seg['name']: seg['importance'] for seg in segments_data}\\n    capacities = {seg['name']: seg['capacity'] for seg in segments_data}\\n    \\n    # While budget remains\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_name = None\\n        best_score = None\\n        # Iterate in original order to break ties by position\\n        for name in names:\\n            if alloc[name] >= capacities[name]:\\n                continue\\n            # Score = importance / (next allocated position = current + 1)\\n            score = importances[name] / (alloc[name] + 1)\\n            if best_name is None or score > best_score:\\n                best_score = score\\n                best_name = name\\n        # If no segment can take more (should not happen if budget <= total_capacity)\\n        if best_name is None:\\n            break\\n        alloc[best_name] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    \\n    # Compute total\\n    total = sum(alloc.values())\\n    # Build result\\n    result = {\\n        'allocations': alloc,\\n        'names': names,\\n        'total': total\\n    }\\n    return result\\n\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a JSON object with key \"implementation\" whose value is a Python source string defining `solve(case)`. The function must implement the described algorithm: allocate budget across segments, each with minimum, capacity, importance. Initialize each at minimum. Then while budget remains, allocate one token to the segment with highest importance / (next allocated position). Tie break by original order (segment index in list). Return a JSON-serializable object with fields: allocations (dict segment name -> allocated tokens), names (list of segment names? Actually \"name mapping\" likely a dict mapping original name to something? The problem says \"Return allocations, the name mapping, and the conserved total.\" Probably allocations dict, name_mapping dict (maybe same as names), total allocated sum. Also need to validate budget >= sum(minimum) and <= total capacity. Raise ValueError if not.\n\nWe must not mutate case. Use only standard library.\n\nImplementation: parse case payload. segments list. For each segment, compute min, capacity, importance. Compute sum_min = sum(segment['minimum'] for segment in segments). total_capacity = sum(segment['capacity']). If budget < sum_min or budget > total_capacity: raise ValueError.\n\nInitialize allocations = {seg['name']: seg['minimum'] for seg in segments}. remaining = budget - sum_min.\n\nWhile remaining > 0: For each segment, compute score = seg['importance'] / (allocations[seg['name']] + 1)  # next position? Actually \"importance divided by its next allocated position\". If we are giving one token, the next allocated position is current allocation + 1 (since we will add one). So score = importance / (current_alloc + 1). Choose segment with max score. In case of tie, choose earliest in original order (by index). Increment that segment's allocation. But must ensure not exceeding capacity. If